    {
      "id": 26326,
      "name": "Christopher",
      "username": "Christopher",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/christopher/{size}/1851_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-11-05T03:16:57.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Respectfully, I disagree. If the card listed a number of cards (such as: \"1 player must discard 1 card to destroy this card\"), then yes, you would have to discard that number of cards. However, if a card says to discard your hand, well, you can discard a hand of zero cards in order to fulfill that requirement. As a player, you always have a hand, even if you happen to have zero cards in hand.</p><p>The only time that this is not true is when your hero is Incapacitated. At that point, you've removed all of your cards from the game and no longer have a hand, unfortunately.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:00:15.640Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
