      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Respectfully, I disagree. If the card listed a number of cards (such as: \"1 player must discard 1 card to destroy this card\"), then yes, you would have to discard that number of cards. However, if a card says to discard your hand, well, you can discard a hand of zero cards in order to fulfill that requirement. As a player, you always have a hand, even if you happen to have zero cards in hand.</p><p>The only time that this is not true is when your hero is Incapacitated. At that point, you've removed all of your cards from the game and no longer have a hand, unfortunately.</p>",
